^["risk_model"]{
 hard_failures: [
  "a move leaves refs or lineage strings pointing at the dated cut or the old shelf folders",
  "the snapshot tag names a commit whose cut differs from the shelved one",
  "a mechanical pass rewrites a claim statement or renames an anchor"
 ]
 soft_failures: [
  "LSP and graph caches keep the old paths until reindexed",
  "open worktrees and plan streams still name the old paths"
 ]
 recoveries: [
  "spw resolve and the cut gate run after every commit; any new unresolved ref blocks the commit",
  "plan streams are history and keep the old paths; cards and roots follow the move",
  "the tag caches-cut/2026.09.30 holds the layout as shelved, so any move can be compared against it"
 ]
 non_negotiables: [
  "no anchor is renamed or reused; the permanence rule holds",
  "claim statements stay byte-identical through mechanical passes",
  "the raw generation moves whole and unchanged; git records every shelf file as a pure rename",
  "the quarantine keeps every file it names",
  "commits and the snapshot tag are authorized by the owner"
 ]
}

^["validation"]{
 hypotheses: [
  "H1 the moves change no anchor and no ref target: 8180 anchors before and after, and the only unresolved refs that change are the three panel refs this plan fixes",
  "H2 the receipt ledger loses nothing: every file, event, at, agent, care, and outcome tuple is recoverable from journal entries",
  "H3 receipts to the journal and a trimmed card cut at least 15 percent of the tree's lines with claim statements byte-identical",
  "H4 an agent given only the extension door and the gate adds one surface to the tree and one entry to the journal, and both pass",
  "H5 anchor-addressed refs remove about 400 thousand characters, about 8 percent of the tree"
 ]
 negative_controls: [
  "git shows every raw shelf file as a 100 percent rename into journal/2026-09-30-gemini-shelf",
  "the quarantine names the same nine files at their new paths",
  "the sorted list of claim statement strings is identical before and after each mechanical pass"
 ]
 demo_path: [
  "open .spw/caches/index.spw and follow the extension door",
  "add one surface to the tree and one entry to the journal in a worktree and run the gate",
  "check out the tag caches-cut/2026.09.30 and find the dated cut and the shelf as they were"
 ]
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] observe — The cut holds 439 files and 86604 lines; 68 percent of its characters sit inside strings. Path refs are 663 thousand characters, about 417 thousand of them path prefix, though anchors are already unique across the cut. The emit and provenance blocks are 14724 lines, receipts 2717 lines. 322 of about 600 concept tags occur once. The cut has no root index; the gate fails on three refs to panels nobody has written; the caches index still routes only to the raw shelf.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The owner chose samples first, then parser changes, for the syntax revision, staged under syntax-hardware-alignment, whose rule is samples before any parser change.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The owner chose a living tree with git-tag snapshots over extending the dated directory in place or opening a new dated cut per pass.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The owner asked for a directory for dated .spw files, a journal. It opens at .spw/journal at the canon root, entries named YYYY-MM-DD-slug.spw; resume notes, snapshot manifests, and receipt ledgers are its first kinds of entry.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] decide — The living tree is .spw/caches/cut; the raw shelf stays where it is, per the owner decision recorded in the caches-cut-2026-09-30 plan.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:08] taste — The contract is 232 lines and every rule in it is real, but an extending agent needs a door of about forty lines: where to put a surface, which exemplar to copy, which namespace to write under, which gate to run, and where its receipt goes.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] decide — The owner took @cut#src_x as the starting ref form, a root figure with a fragment; the root names the layer, so refs read @tree#src_x and @journal#entry_anchor, with both roots declared once in .spw/workspace.spw.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] decide — The owner approved caches-cut/2026.09.30 on main at 813444dc as the snapshot tag. Later snapshots of the living tree are tagged caches/YYYY.MM.DD.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] observe — Time binds unevenly: 53 surfaces mark era current, 111 carry 296 as_of lines outside provenance, and all 631 quantity cells carry an at. Season holds recurring forms (arc, retrospective protocol, festivals, fiscal and academic years, the journal template) and one dated instance, the 2026 Q4 calendar with its trail.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] revise — Putting season files in the journal moved the line: the journal is not a side folder for notes but the dated layer of the caches. A surface belongs in the tree when someone should edit it to keep it true, and in the journal when it records what was seen or made on a day and is never edited after. The tree becomes a view over the journal and the sources.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] decide — The owner chose that structure inside .spw/caches: index.spw and extend.spw at the root, tree/ for the living synthesis, journal/ for dated append-only entries. The raw generation becomes one journal entry, journal/2026-09-30-gemini-shelf, moved whole; this revises the earlier decision that the shelf stays in its topic folders, and nothing is deleted. The canon-root journal from 10:08 is dropped.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] decide — The living layer is named tree, not cut; a cut is a dated selection and this layer is not one.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:17] decide — Only the season instance moves: calendar-2026q4 and trails/season-2026-q4 become journal/2026-10-01-season-2026-q4; the recurring season forms stay in tree/season.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:21] implement — Tagged main at 813444dc as caches-cut/2026.09.30, annotated, local. Opened .spw/caches/journal with its contract and seven entry kinds; the resume note moved in whole as 2026-09-30-resume.spw, and the snapshot manifest is 2026-10-13-cut-snapshot.spw. The workspace declares @caches and @journal; @tree waits for the move.
 >>[2026-10-13 10:21] decide — The resume note moved in unchanged, so its not_in_this_revision frame now goes stale with the move. Under the append-only rule a new resume entry supersedes it rather than an edit; ~[root_door] writes it.
}

